 48 luma rows of 720, all exact multiples of 16 -- and the count VARIES between
 frames, which rules out a fixed dimension or stride error and points at the
 decoder running out of something.

 The loop at 2379aac has exactly two exits:

     2379ab0  bge   block counter exhausted   (normal end of plane)
     2379ac0  bge   cur >= end                (ran out of bitstream)

 Instrument both so the log says which one fires, and with what pointers.

